Sparky Stereo OS: the 3D viewer draws its OpenGL view as a stereo pair, two parallel cameras with an off-axis frustum (a shear in the orthographic view), into a quad buffer that the edition's Mesa hands to Stereo KWin as declared full side by side.
The separation is the person's depth limits, read from the desktop through libstereo-declare: the largest under which every pixel of the view stays inside them; no separation setting. Without limits both eyes are the same picture and the info bar says why, once.
The 3D viewer's 3D options are Enable 3D (on by default) and a button to Display Settings; the new sentences in the ten languages (translations/kicad-3d-viewer-stereo.po.patch).
Build-Depends on libstereo-declare-dev (>= 1.11.0); the source and the kicad package are built, the architecture-independent packages stay Debian's.
KiCad's QA test programs are not built (-DKICAD_BUILD_QA_TESTS=OFF in debian/rules): they are never run in this build and install nothing.
A translucent 3D model counts in that fit by its share of each pixel: the pass that measures the depth is drawn off screen, where each pixel ends as the mean distance of what it shows, each weighted by its share of the pixel's colour.
Rules-Requires-Root: no, so the Lean Code gate's bubblewrap is not started under fakeroot; Debian's rules change no owner and every file stays root:root.
